---
title: Pastrami sandwich
servings: 1
yield: 1 sandwich
tags: [beef, smoker, make-ahead]
source: The OG by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/the-og
---

> The pastrami is a whole brisket cured for three weeks; the sandwich uses
> 8 oz of it.

== Pastrami ==

In an #18-quart container{}, whisk @pink curing salt{}(Cure no. 1),
@kosher salt{} and @granulated sugar{} into @water{}(filtered). Add the
@black peppercorns{}(whole), @coriander seeds{}, @mustard seeds{}(yellow),
@cinnamon sticks{} and @bay leaves{}.

Sink the @brisket{1}(whole, trimmed to a ¼-inch fat cap, halved) in the brine,
weighted if needed. Cover and refrigerate ~{21%days}, turning it every
~{3%days}.

Rinse and pat dry. Heat the #smoker{} to 250°F.

Rub the brisket with @deli mustard{}, then season with @ground coriander{},
@smoked paprika{} and @black pepper{}(ground). Smoke ~{6%hours}, until a bark
forms.

Set it on a rack in a #roasting pan{} with a little water underneath and cover
tightly with foil. Heat the oven to 250°F and roast to an internal 200°F.

Rest ~{1%hour}, then slice.

== Thousand Island dressing ==

Mix the @mayonnaise{100%g} and @ketchup{100%g} with some @dill pickles{}(minced)
and @onion{}(minced). Season with @lemon juice{}, @granulated sugar{},
@kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}(ground). Refrigerate.

== Slaw dressing ==

Blend the @red wine vinegar{2%cups}, @extra virgin olive oil{1%cup},
@garlic{3%tbsp}(minced), @onion{3%tbsp}(minced) and @honey{1%tsp} in a
#blender{}. Season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}(ground).
Refrigerate.

== Cabbage slaw ==

Toss the @purple cabbage{1%head}(shredded),
@parsley{1%bunch}(leaves, chopped) and @dill{1%bunch}(fronds, chopped)
with some of the slaw dressing. Leave ~{10%minutes}.

== Sandwich ==

Heat the oven to 250°F. Warm 8 oz of the pastrami on a foil-lined
#sheet tray{}.

Butter both sides of the @rye bread{2%slices} with @unsalted butter{} and
toast in a #sauté pan{} over medium heat until golden.

Spread @deli mustard{} on one slice and Thousand Island dressing on the other.
Pile on the slaw, the @Swiss cheese{1%slice} and the pastrami.

Close, wrap in #wax paper{}, and cut in half.
